  "idea": "exp(-i theta Z_j (b + b^+)) for a mode b that is grid-adjacent to but not the home mode of qubit j: conjugate an ordinary home-mode displacement by a full conditional beam splitter CBS(pi,0) on (j; home, b). The Hadamard lemma closes after one commutator (ad_G^2 = identity on span{a,b}), so U maps the home-mode annihilation operator onto i*Z_j*b exactly (all photon numbers, no truncation error). Conjugating D(beta) on the home mode therefore produces exactly the Z_j-conditioned displacement of the target mode, with beta = -theta chosen to match the stated coefficient. No ancilla; no router SWAP of the remote mode is needed.",
